<title>RUSSIA: Mosenergo plans $100-150 mln Eurobond.</title>
<headline>Mosenergo plans $100-150 mln Eurobond.</headline>
<dateline>MOSCOW 1996-12-05</dateline>
<text>
<p>Moscow regional power utility Mosenergo plans to issue a $100-150 million Eurobond in the first quarter of 1997, chief executive Nestor Serebryanikov said on Thursday.</p>
<p>&quot;It will be $100-150 million, but most of us think it will be $150 million,&quot; he told a news conference.  </p>
<p>The bond will be led by Salomon Bros.</p>
<p>Eugene Tenebaum, vice president of Salomon Bros International, said the maturity would probably be five years.</p>
<p>Salomon Bros managed a private placement of American Depositary Receipts (ADRs) for Mosenergo last year.</p>
<p>--Olga Popova, Moscow Newsroom, +7095 941 8520</p>
